From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stage C <stage-c@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:05:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: inline small constant memory intrinsics

cg_clif lowered every `memcpy`, `memmove` and `memset` to a libc call and
never looked at the size. The hot 8-byte swaps in core's sort therefore called
`compiler_builtins`' `copy_forward` (157 instructions per swap) where LLVM
emits an i64 load and store.

Read the constant count from the MIR operand and put the decision in one
helper used by all four lowering sites: size 0 emits nothing; a constant size
up to 64 bytes becomes straight-line loads followed by stores (memmove
semantics, widest power-of-two width that divides the size, aligned only when
the pointee's alignment guarantees it); a larger or runtime size becomes
`memory.copy`/`memory.fill` when the target has bulk-memory (wasm32 unless
`-bulk-memory`); otherwise it stays a libc call. Volatile operations keep the
libc call.

sort's instruction count drops from 1.26G to 327M (8.39x to 2.17x LLVM -O2)
in bench/gap, and no `memcpy`/`memmove`/`memset` call remains in its hot
functions.
